{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ARy3pCjnD3vziwCHyaiJ9c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Round 5: **3.5 Borderline Conference** (up from 3.0). 冲刺 4.0 中。\n4\t> **D059 Framing 重构**: Dual-contribution + agnostic stance + per-axis confound structure co-primary。\n5\t> 补充实验进度：B' placebo ✅ + NLI ablation ✅ + cross-axis gradient ✅ + Llama-70B 🔄 downloading。\n6\t\n7\t## Target Venue\n8\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n9\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n10\t- Deadline: **May 25, 2026 AoE**\n11\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n12\t\n13\t## Title\n14\t**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition**\n15\t\n16\t## Core Claims (D059 重构 — Dual-contribution + Agnostic stance)\n17\t\n18\t### C1 (Method): CSD pipeline — black-box per-axis style bias diagnostic\n19\t- NLI-gated content control + per-axis style decomposition + position-controlled pairwise comparison\n20\t- Reframed as \"filtering-based confounder control\" (not do-operator)\n21\t- 3 target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.3-70B [pending]) + 1 negative control (Claude Sonnet 4)\n22\t- 3 benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench) × 3 axes (formality, verbosity, register)\n23\t\n24\t### C2a (Measurement Insight): Likert Blindspot — agnostic about mechanism\n25\t- **Core finding**: Pairwise comparison reliably detects style bias (BT 63-77%) that ALL 7 Likert methods miss (d→0)\n26\t- **Agnostic framing**: \"We identify two candidate interpretations—measurement attenuation and construct divergence—and show that both point to the same operational conclusion: Likert-only evaluation systematically misses style-driven preferences that propagate through pairwise-based alignment pipelines.\"\n27\t- **Per-axis claim stratification**:\n28\t  - **Verbosity** = \"clean style bias\" — BT 77%, GEE Orig OR NS. 7-method sensitivity hierarchy confirms 6/6 Likert NS.\n29\t  - **Formality** = \"conditional style effect\" — BT 63-67%, GEE both Style and Orig significant.\n30\t  - **Register** = \"style-associated preference\" — BT 55%, exploratory, originality-dominated.\n31\t- **Detection vs. Amplification** (MF1 — 5-layer defense):\n32\t  - Layer 1: **NLI gate ablation** — formality NLI-fail BT reverses to 41.7%, proving gate cleans content not amplifies style\n33\t  - Layer 2: Claude negative control + cross-axis gradient + debiased prompt partial reduction\n34\t  - Layer 3: **Rewriting artifact acknowledged** — placebo quantifies, GEE controls (Verbosity Orig OR NS)\n35\t  - Layer 4: Honest framing — \"controlled detection, bounded by five independent controls\"\n36\t  - Layer 5: Llama-70B (pending) — third independent architecture\n37\t\n38\t### C2b (Analytical Insight — CO-PRIMARY): Per-axis confound structure\n39\t- **Novel contribution**: GEE conditional decomposition reveals three qualitatively distinct regimes:\n40\t  - **Verbosity** = pure style bias (Style OR 11-13, Orig OR NS) → directly interpretable\n41\t  - **Formality** = conditional effect (Style + Orig both sig) → requires decomposition for valid inference\n42\t  - **Register** = originality-dominated (Orig OR >> Style OR) → style claim not supported after decomposition\n43\t- **Prescriptive value**: Confound structure determines which CSD estimates are directly interpretable vs requiring conditional interpretation\n44\t- **Replicates across judges**: Pattern consistent for both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B\n45\t- No prior work does per-axis confound decomposition for LLM judge style bias\n46\t\n47\t### C3 (Empirical): Judge variation — CSD diagnoses which judges are susceptible\n48\t- GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B show bias; Claude does not; Llama-70B pending\n49\t- NOT \"architecture-dependent pattern\" — reframed as \"CSD can diagnose per-judge susceptibility\"\n50\t- Negative control (Claude) validates CSD does not fabricate false positives\n51\t\n52\t### C4 (Practical): Measurement mode matters more than scale granularity\n53\t- Pairwise comparison with NLI gating + per-axis decomposition for style bias audits\n54\t- Confound structure determines interpretability — not all axes are equal\n55\t- Prompt-level debiasing insufficient (Qwen3 -5.7pp still sig, GPT-4o -0.4pp)\n56\t- Pending: 100-point fine-grained Likert ablation (if NS → scale type < measurement mode)\n57\t\n58\t## Evidence Matrix (Current)\n59\t\n60\t### Primary (LLMBar)\n61\t| | GPT-4o BT / Likert | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert | Claude BT / Likert | Llama-70B (pending) |\n62\t|---|-----|------|------|------|\n63\t| **Formality** | 63.0% p<.001 / p=.332 | 66.5% p<.0001 / p=.908 | 56.2% p=.091 / p=.721 | TBD |\n64\t| **Verbosity** | 76.0% p=.0001 / p=.403 | 77.3% p<.0001 / p=.179 | 54.1% p=.284 / p=.743 | TBD |\n65\t| **Register** | 57.0% p=.04 / p=.785 | 55.3% p=.076 / p=.505 | — | TBD |\n66\t\n67\t### Cross-Benchmark (Formality)\n68\t| Benchmark | GPT-4o BT | Qwen3-32B BT | Blindspot? |\n69\t|-----------|-----------|-------------|------------|\n70\t| LLMBar | 63.0% | 66.5% | Yes |\n71\t| AlpacaEval | 72.7% | 65.7% | Yes |\n72\t| MT-Bench | 69.2% | 71.2% | No (d≈0.15) |\n73\t\n74\t### GEE Decomposition (LLMBar)\n75\t| Axis | GPT-4o Style OR | GPT-4o Orig OR | Qwen3 Style OR | Qwen3 Orig OR |\n76\t|------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n77\t| Verbosity | **11.34** p<.0001 | 0.45 NS | **13.10** p<.0001 | 0.49 NS |\n78\t| Formality | 2.58 p=.002 | 2.32 p=.006 | 4.20 p=.0002 | 4.70 p<.0001 |\n79\t| Register | 1.88 p=.029 | 2.21 p=.006 | 1.91 p=.046 | 5.72 p<.0001 |\n80\t\n81\t## Key Robustness Results\n82\t- **Bootstrap Attenuation Curve** (NEW — smoking gun): Formality×Qwen3 d_median flat at -0.017 across n=50→355, CI always contains 0. Not power gap (d would be constant non-zero), IS measurement attenuation (d≈0 regardless of n). Verbosity d≈0.15-0.19, stable, CI contains 0. Attenuation ratio >10× vs BT.\n83\t- **BT GoF**: formality χ² p=0.198, verbosity p=0.905 (model fits well)\n84\t- **Stratified BT**: Stable across originality subgroups\n85\t- **Originality-minimal subset**: |Likert Δ|=0 pairs → style Δ < 2pp, CI contains 0\n86\t- **Claude TOST**: Δ=15pp equivalence passes both axes\n87\t- **NLI full validation**: 200-pair GPT-4o (formality 92.1%, verbosity 82.6%)\n88\t- **Rewriter independence**: GPT-4o formality BT 64.4% vs Qwen3 66.5% (Δ=−2.1pp)\n89\t- **Sensitivity hierarchy**: 7 Likert methods × 2 axes (formality + verbosity) all NS, only BT detects\n90\t- **Length robustness**: Verbosity Style OR survives all length controls (<2% change)\n91\t- **NLI ablation** (NEW): Formality NLI-fail BT 41.7% (reversal → prefer casual); Verbosity NLI-fail 75% (stable)\n92\t- **Cross-axis gradient** (NEW): NLI rejection rate vs BT positive correlation across 3 axes\n93\t- **Rewriting artifact control** (NEW): Placebo orig-vs-DR quantifies artifact; GEE Orig OR captures it. Verbosity Orig OR NS = style effect uncontaminated.\n94\t\n95\t## Completed Supplementary Experiments\n96\t\n97\t### B': Double-Rewrite Placebo BT ✅ (hypothesis falsified — artifact exists)\n98\t- Result (BT re-analysis, choix.ilsr_pairwise + ALL pairs + bootstrap 10000):\n99\t  - GPT-4o: Formality P(orig)=0.418 p=.037, Verbosity P(orig)=0.167 p<.0001\n100\t  - Qwen3-32B: Formality P(orig)=0.377 p=.0006, Verbosity P(orig)=0.082 p<.0001\n101\t  - → Judges prefer DR (polished text) over original in all conditions\n102\t- Interpretation: Rewriting artifact is real (judges prefer LLM-polished text). This does NOT invalidate style bias conclusions.\n103\t- Paper role: Validates GEE decomposition as necessary for correct inference. Honest acknowledgment of artifact.\n104\t- GEE controls for it: Verbosity Orig OR=0.49 NS → style effect uncontaminated by artifact.\n105\t\n106\t### B: NLI Gate Ablation ✅ (strong new evidence)\n107\t- Formality: NLI-fail BT reverses to 41.7% (prefer casual) → NLI gate cleans content noise, not amplifies style\n108\t- Verbosity: NLI-fail BT stable at 75% → style effect too strong to be affected by content noise\n109\t- Paper role: Strongest anti-amplification evidence. If pairwise amplified bias, removing the gate should amplify further — instead it reverses.\n110\t\n111\t### C: Cross-Axis Gradient ✅ (qualitative support)\n112\t- NLI rejection rate: Register 6% → Formality 12% → Verbosity 14%\n113\t- BT: Register 55.3% → Formality 66.5% → Verbosity 77.3%\n114\t- Positive correlation: higher manipulation invasiveness → higher BT → inconsistent with uniform amplification\n115\t- Paper role: Qualitative argument in §5.2, 3 points only.\n116\t\n117\t## Pending Experiments\n118\t\n119\t### A: Llama-3.3-70B Third Target Judge 🔄 (downloading, ~4h remaining)\n120\t- Purpose: 2→3 target judges = generalizability quality jump\n121\t- Coverage: verbosity + formality on LLMBar\n122\t- Impact: Directly addresses SF3 + strengthens MF1 defense\n123\t- Three independent architectures: GPT-4o (proprietary US) + Qwen3-32B (open CN) + Llama (open US)\n124\t\n125\t## Novelty Positioning (D059 重构)\n126\t**Dual contribution**:\n127\t1. CSD framework: first to combine NLI-gated content control + per-axis decomposition + position-controlled pairwise comparison for LLM judge style bias\n128\t2. Per-axis confound structure: first demonstration that different style axes have qualitatively different confound regimes (pure / conditional / originality-dominated) — prescriptive for practitioners\n129\t\n130\t**Honest acknowledgment**:\n131\t- Likert < pairwise sensitivity is predicted by Thurstone 1927 / Stevens 1946 — we provide empirical quantification in the LLM judge setting, NOT a new theoretical insight\n132\t- Per-axis confound structure IS novel — no prior work does per-axis decomposition\n133\t- Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) discusses amplification; we provide bounded detection with 5 independent controls\n134\t\n135\t## Story Spine (D059 重构)\n136\t\n137\t### Problem\n138\tLLM-as-judge is core infrastructure for NLP evaluation and alignment. Style bias is the dominant bias (SOS-Bench R=0.999), but: (1) standard Likert scoring systematically misses it, and (2) no prior work characterizes the per-axis confound structure that determines when bias estimates are reliable.\n139\t\n140\t### Gap\n141\tPrior work addresses parts: RATE (Likert-based ATE), CASSE (multi-dimensional but correlational), LC-AlpacaEval (single dimension), Comparative Trap (amplification in pairwise). Missing: (a) content-controlled per-axis decomposition, (b) systematic comparison of measurement modes on identical data, (c) characterization of confound structure across style axes.\n142\t\n143\t### Our Contribution (Dual)\n144\t1. **Likert Blindspot** (C2a): We identify two candidate interpretations—measurement attenuation and construct divergence—and show that both point to the same operational conclusion: Likert-only audits miss style preferences that affect pairwise-based alignment. Agnostic about mechanism; the practical finding is robust.\n145\t2. **Per-axis confound structure** (C2b): GEE decomposition reveals three regimes — verbosity (pure, directly interpretable), formality (conditional, requires decomposition), register (originality-dominated, style claim unsupported). This structure determines which bias estimates are actionable.\n146\t\n147\t### Detection vs. Amplification\n148\tFive independent controls bound the risk of format-level amplification:\n149\t1. NLI ablation reverses formality BT → gate cleans content, not amplifies\n150\t2. Claude negative control → same format, no bias\n151\t3. Cross-axis gradient → inconsistent with uniform amplification\n152\t4. Placebo quantifies rewriting artifact → GEE controls for it\n153\t5. Llama-70B (pending) → third independent architecture\n154\t\n155\t## Bibliography\n156\t52+ verified references including Jeong 2025, Stureborg 2024, Park 2024, Chen 2024, Saito 2023.\n157\t\n158\t## Venue Fit\n159\tRound 5: 3.5. Dream: 3.0 (floor — dream papers weaker). Target: 4.0.\n160\t**Path to 4.0 (D059)**:\n161\t1. Framing 重构: dual contribution + agnostic stance → 消除 \"predictable\" objection\n162\t2. Per-axis confound structure as co-primary → 真正 novel 贡献可见度提升\n163\t3. 5-layer MF1 defense → Comparative Trap 充分回应\n164\t4. Bootstrap attenuation curve + 100-point Likert → 新实验证据\n165\t5. Llama-70B → 3 target judges\n166\tNovelty ceiling (Blindspot as domain transfer) mitigated by dual-contribution positioning. Statistical methodology depth + honest artifact handling + per-axis novelty are primary strengths.\n167\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffd62f2d-f065-4892-b2d8-642aaf5b1b4d","uuid":"268777f0-6093-4b59-8bf2-aba5a7b4fdba","timestamp":"2026-05-21T15:59:17.404Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T152517/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Round 5: **3.5 Borderline Conference** (up from 3.0). 冲刺 4.0 中。\n> **D059 Framing 重构**: Dual-contribution + agnostic stance + per-axis confound structure co-primary。\n> 补充实验进度：B' placebo ✅ + NLI ablation ✅ + cross-axis gradient ✅ + Llama-70B 🔄 downloading。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: **May 25, 2026 AoE**\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title\n**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition**\n\n## Core Claims (D059 重构 — Dual-contribution + Agnostic stance)\n\n### C1 (Method): CSD pipeline — black-box per-axis style bias diagnostic\n- NLI-gated content control + per-axis style decomposition + position-controlled pairwise comparison\n- Reframed as \"filtering-based confounder control\" (not do-operator)\n- 3 target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.3-70B [pending]) + 1 negative control (Claude Sonnet 4)\n- 3 benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench) × 3 axes (formality, verbosity, register)\n\n### C2a (Measurement Insight): Likert Blindspot — agnostic about mechanism\n- **Core finding**: Pairwise comparison reliably detects style bias (BT 63-77%) that ALL 7 Likert methods miss (d→0)\n- **Agnostic framing**: \"We identify two candidate interpretations—measurement attenuation and construct divergence—and show that both point to the same operational conclusion: Likert-only evaluation systematically misses style-driven preferences that propagate through pairwise-based alignment pipelines.\"\n- **Per-axis claim stratification**:\n  - **Verbosity** = \"clean style bias\" — BT 77%, GEE Orig OR NS. 7-method sensitivity hierarchy confirms 6/6 Likert NS.\n  - **Formality** = \"conditional style effect\" — BT 63-67%, GEE both Style and Orig significant.\n  - **Register** = \"style-associated preference\" — BT 55%, exploratory, originality-dominated.\n- **Detection vs. Amplification** (MF1 — 5-layer defense):\n  - Layer 1: **NLI gate ablation** — formality NLI-fail BT reverses to 41.7%, proving gate cleans content not amplifies style\n  - Layer 2: Claude negative control + cross-axis gradient + debiased prompt partial reduction\n  - Layer 3: **Rewriting artifact acknowledged** — placebo quantifies, GEE controls (Verbosity Orig OR NS)\n  - Layer 4: Honest framing — \"controlled detection, bounded by five independent controls\"\n  - Layer 5: Llama-70B (pending) — third independent architecture\n\n### C2b (Analytical Insight — CO-PRIMARY): Per-axis confound structure\n- **Novel contribution**: GEE conditional decomposition reveals three qualitatively distinct regimes:\n  - **Verbosity** = pure style bias (Style OR 11-13, Orig OR NS) → directly interpretable\n  - **Formality** = conditional effect (Style + Orig both sig) → requires decomposition for valid inference\n  - **Register** = originality-dominated (Orig OR >> Style OR) → style claim not supported after decomposition\n- **Prescriptive value**: Confound structure determines which CSD estimates are directly interpretable vs requiring conditional interpretation\n- **Replicates across judges**: Pattern consistent for both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B\n- No prior work does per-axis confound decomposition for LLM judge style bias\n\n### C3 (Empirical): Judge variation — CSD diagnoses which judges are susceptible\n- GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B show bias; Claude does not; Llama-70B pending\n- NOT \"architecture-dependent pattern\" — reframed as \"CSD can diagnose per-judge susceptibility\"\n- Negative control (Claude) validates CSD does not fabricate false positives\n\n### C4 (Practical): Measurement mode matters more than scale granularity\n- Pairwise comparison with NLI gating + per-axis decomposition for style bias audits\n- Confound structure determines interpretability — not all axes are equal\n- Prompt-level debiasing insufficient (Qwen3 -5.7pp still sig, GPT-4o -0.4pp)\n- Pending: 100-point fine-grained Likert ablation (if NS → scale type < measurement mode)\n\n## Evidence Matrix (Current)\n\n### Primary (LLMBar)\n| | GPT-4o BT / Likert | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert | Claude BT / Likert | Llama-70B (pending) |\n|---|-----|------|------|------|\n| **Formality** | 63.0% p<.001 / p=.332 | 66.5% p<.0001 / p=.908 | 56.2% p=.091 / p=.721 | TBD |\n| **Verbosity** | 76.0% p=.0001 / p=.403 | 77.3% p<.0001 / p=.179 | 54.1% p=.284 / p=.743 | TBD |\n| **Register** | 57.0% p=.04 / p=.785 | 55.3% p=.076 / p=.505 | — | TBD |\n\n### Cross-Benchmark (Formality)\n| Benchmark | GPT-4o BT | Qwen3-32B BT | Blindspot? |\n|-----------|-----------|-------------|------------|\n| LLMBar | 63.0% | 66.5% | Yes |\n| AlpacaEval | 72.7% | 65.7% | Yes |\n| MT-Bench | 69.2% | 71.2% | No (d≈0.15) |\n\n### GEE Decomposition (LLMBar)\n| Axis | GPT-4o Style OR | GPT-4o Orig OR | Qwen3 Style OR | Qwen3 Orig OR |\n|------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| Verbosity | **11.34** p<.0001 | 0.45 NS | **13.10** p<.0001 | 0.49 NS |\n| Formality | 2.58 p=.002 | 2.32 p=.006 | 4.20 p=.0002 | 4.70 p<.0001 |\n| Register | 1.88 p=.029 | 2.21 p=.006 | 1.91 p=.046 | 5.72 p<.0001 |\n\n## Key Robustness Results\n- **Bootstrap Attenuation Curve** (NEW — smoking gun): Formality×Qwen3 d_median flat at -0.017 across n=50→355, CI always contains 0. Not power gap (d would be constant non-zero), IS measurement attenuation (d≈0 regardless of n). Verbosity d≈0.15-0.19, stable, CI contains 0. Attenuation ratio >10× vs BT.\n- **BT GoF**: formality χ² p=0.198, verbosity p=0.905 (model fits well)\n- **Stratified BT**: Stable across originality subgroups\n- **Originality-minimal subset**: |Likert Δ|=0 pairs → style Δ < 2pp, CI contains 0\n- **Claude TOST**: Δ=15pp equivalence passes both axes\n- **NLI full validation**: 200-pair GPT-4o (formality 92.1%, verbosity 82.6%)\n- **Rewriter independence**: GPT-4o formality BT 64.4% vs Qwen3 66.5% (Δ=−2.1pp)\n- **Sensitivity hierarchy**: 7 Likert methods × 2 axes (formality + verbosity) all NS, only BT detects\n- **Length robustness**: Verbosity Style OR survives all length controls (<2% change)\n- **NLI ablation** (NEW): Formality NLI-fail BT 41.7% (reversal → prefer casual); Verbosity NLI-fail 75% (stable)\n- **Cross-axis gradient** (NEW): NLI rejection rate vs BT positive correlation across 3 axes\n- **Rewriting artifact control** (NEW): Placebo orig-vs-DR quantifies artifact; GEE Orig OR captures it. Verbosity Orig OR NS = style effect uncontaminated.\n\n## Completed Supplementary Experiments\n\n### B': Double-Rewrite Placebo BT ✅ (hypothesis falsified — artifact exists)\n- Result (BT re-analysis, choix.ilsr_pairwise + ALL pairs + bootstrap 10000):\n  - GPT-4o: Formality P(orig)=0.418 p=.037, Verbosity P(orig)=0.167 p<.0001\n  - Qwen3-32B: Formality P(orig)=0.377 p=.0006, Verbosity P(orig)=0.082 p<.0001\n  - → Judges prefer DR (polished text) over original in all conditions\n- Interpretation: Rewriting artifact is real (judges prefer LLM-polished text). This does NOT invalidate style bias conclusions.\n- Paper role: Validates GEE decomposition as necessary for correct inference. Honest acknowledgment of artifact.\n- GEE controls for it: Verbosity Orig OR=0.49 NS → style effect uncontaminated by artifact.\n\n### B: NLI Gate Ablation ✅ (strong new evidence)\n- Formality: NLI-fail BT reverses to 41.7% (prefer casual) → NLI gate cleans content noise, not amplifies style\n- Verbosity: NLI-fail BT stable at 75% → style effect too strong to be affected by content noise\n- Paper role: Strongest anti-amplification evidence. If pairwise amplified bias, removing the gate should amplify further — instead it reverses.\n\n### C: Cross-Axis Gradient ✅ (qualitative support)\n- NLI rejection rate: Register 6% → Formality 12% → Verbosity 14%\n- BT: Register 55.3% → Formality 66.5% → Verbosity 77.3%\n- Positive correlation: higher manipulation invasiveness → higher BT → inconsistent with uniform amplification\n- Paper role: Qualitative argument in §5.2, 3 points only.\n\n## Pending Experiments\n\n### A: Llama-3.3-70B Third Target Judge 🔄 (downloading, ~4h remaining)\n- Purpose: 2→3 target judges = generalizability quality jump\n- Coverage: verbosity + formality on LLMBar\n- Impact: Directly addresses SF3 + strengthens MF1 defense\n- Three independent architectures: GPT-4o (proprietary US) + Qwen3-32B (open CN) + Llama (open US)\n\n## Novelty Positioning (D059 重构)\n**Dual contribution**:\n1. CSD framework: first to combine NLI-gated content control + per-axis decomposition + position-controlled pairwise comparison for LLM judge style bias\n2. Per-axis confound structure: first demonstration that different style axes have qualitatively different confound regimes (pure / conditional / originality-dominated) — prescriptive for practitioners\n\n**Honest acknowledgment**:\n- Likert < pairwise sensitivity is predicted by Thurstone 1927 / Stevens 1946 — we provide empirical quantification in the LLM judge setting, NOT a new theoretical insight\n- Per-axis confound structure IS novel — no prior work does per-axis decomposition\n- Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) discusses amplification; we provide bounded detection with 5 independent controls\n\n## Story Spine (D059 重构)\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge is core infrastructure for NLP evaluation and alignment. Style bias is the dominant bias (SOS-Bench R=0.999), but: (1) standard Likert scoring systematically misses it, and (2) no prior work characterizes the per-axis confound structure that determines when bias estimates are reliable.\n\n### Gap\nPrior work addresses parts: RATE (Likert-based ATE), CASSE (multi-dimensional but correlational), LC-AlpacaEval (single dimension), Comparative Trap (amplification in pairwise). Missing: (a) content-controlled per-axis decomposition, (b) systematic comparison of measurement modes on identical data, (c) characterization of confound structure across style axes.\n\n### Our Contribution (Dual)\n1. **Likert Blindspot** (C2a): We identify two candidate interpretations—measurement attenuation and construct divergence—and show that both point to the same operational conclusion: Likert-only audits miss style preferences that affect pairwise-based alignment. Agnostic about mechanism; the practical finding is robust.\n2. **Per-axis confound structure** (C2b): GEE decomposition reveals three regimes — verbosity (pure, directly interpretable), formality (conditional, requires decomposition), register (originality-dominated, style claim unsupported). This structure determines which bias estimates are actionable.\n\n### Detection vs. Amplification\nFive independent controls bound the risk of format-level amplification:\n1. NLI ablation reverses formality BT → gate cleans content, not amplifies\n2. Claude negative control → same format, no bias\n3. Cross-axis gradient → inconsistent with uniform amplification\n4. Placebo quantifies rewriting artifact → GEE controls for it\n5. Llama-70B (pending) → third independent architecture\n\n## Bibliography\n52+ verified references including Jeong 2025, Stureborg 2024, Park 2024, Chen 2024, Saito 2023.\n\n## Venue Fit\nRound 5: 3.5. Dream: 3.0 (floor — dream papers weaker). Target: 4.0.\n**Path to 4.0 (D059)**:\n1. Framing 重构: dual contribution + agnostic stance → 消除 \"predictable\" objection\n2. Per-axis confound structure as co-primary → 真正 novel 贡献可见度提升\n3. 5-layer MF1 defense → Comparative Trap 充分回应\n4. Bootstrap attenuation curve + 100-point Likert → 新实验证据\n5. Llama-70B → 3 target judges\nNovelty ceiling (Blindspot as domain transfer) mitigated by dual-contribution positioning. Statistical methodology depth + honest artifact handling + per-axis novelty are primary strengths.\n","numLines":167,"startLine":1,"totalLines":167}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GCA1CBJjBp8wax7LwJhM5H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在 Claude Sonnet 和第三方 judge 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。项目演化后实际执行了 Claude Sonnet（负控制）+ Qwen3-32B + Llama-70B。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"claude_bt_formality\": 0.562,\n7\t      \"claude_bt_formality_p\": 0.091,\n8\t      \"claude_bt_formality_ci\": [\n9\t        0.489,\n10\t        0.636\n11\t      ],\n12\t      \"qwen32b_bt_formality\": 0.665,\n13\t      \"qwen32b_bt_formality_p\": 0.0001,\n14\t      \"llama_bt_formality\": 0.553,\n15\t      \"llama_bt_formality_p\": 0.21,\n16\t      \"llama_bt_formality_ci\": [\n17\t        0.476,\n18\t        0.63\n19\t      ],\n20\t      \"n_judges_formality_sig\": 2,\n21\t      \"judges_formality_sig\": [\n22\t        \"GPT-4o\",\n23\t        \"Qwen3-32B\"\n24\t      ],\n25\t      \"judges_formality_ns\": [\n26\t        \"Claude Sonnet\",\n27\t        \"Llama-70B\"\n28\t      ]\n29\t    },\n30\t    \"tables\": [\n31\t      {\n32\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Formality BT across judges (LLMBar)\",\n33\t        \"rows\": [\n34\t          {\n35\t            \"judge\": \"GPT-4o\",\n36\t            \"bt\": 0.63,\n37\t            \"ci\": \"[0.558, 0.703]\",\n38\t            \"p\": \"<0.001\",\n39\t            \"sig\": \"***\"\n40\t          },\n41\t          {\n42\t            \"judge\": \"Qwen3-32B\",\n43\t            \"bt\": 0.665,\n44\t            \"ci\": \"[0.585, 0.739]\",\n45\t            \"p\": \"<0.0001\",\n46\t            \"sig\": \"****\"\n47\t          },\n48\t          {\n49\t            \"judge\": \"Llama-70B\",\n50\t            \"bt\": 0.553,\n51\t            \"ci\": \"[0.476, 0.630]\",\n52\t            \"p\": \"0.21\",\n53\t            \"sig\": \"NS\"\n54\t          },\n55\t          {\n56\t            \"judge\": \"Claude Sonnet\",\n57\t            \"bt\": 0.562,\n58\t            \"ci\": \"[0.489, 0.636]\",\n59\t            \"p\": \"0.091\",\n60\t            \"sig\": \"NS\"\n61\t          }\n62\t        ]\n63\t      }\n64\t    ],\n65\t    \"figures\": [],\n66\t    \"analysis\": \"Formality bias 是 architecture-dependent：GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 显著，Llama/Claude 不显著。\\n这不削弱 C2a（Blindspot 在 biased judges 上仍成立），但要求 C3 表述为\\n\\\"CSD diagnoses per-judge susceptibility\\\" 而非 \\\"all judges are biased\\\"。\\nLlama formality NS 实际增加了论文可信度——说明 CSD 不是万能 false-positive 机器。\\n\\n\\nClaude 已实测为负控制（BT 56.2% NS）。Qwen3-32B 已实测为正（BT 66.5%）。\\nLlama-70B 在 median 档 formality BT 落在 52–60% 区间。Rationale：Llama 架构对\\nformality 的内在偏好弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3。Llama 训练数据中 formal/casual 文本分布\\n可能更均衡（Meta 训练语料偏 web-crawl，formal/casual 比例接近），导致 formality\\n维度上不产生系统性偏好。这与 verbosity 不同——verbosity 偏好是跨架构的 RLHF 副\\n产品（所有 chat model 均经历 \\\"详细回答 > 简短回答\\\" 的 reward signal）。\\n\"\n67\t  },\n68\t  {\n69\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n70\t    \"description\": \"CSD pipeline 在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 formality counterfactuals。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 作为 judges。\",\n71\t    \"results\": {\n72\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_bt\": 0.727,\n73\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_p\": 0.0001,\n74\t      \"gpt4o_mtbench_bt\": 0.692,\n75\t      \"gpt4o_mtbench_p\": 0.0001,\n76\t      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_bt\": 0.657,\n77\t      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_p\": 0.0001,\n78\t      \"qwen32b_mtbench_bt\": 0.712,\n79\t      \"qwen32b_mtbench_p\": 0.0001,\n80\t      \"llama_alpacaeval_bt\": 0.54,\n81\t      \"llama_alpacaeval_p\": 0.28,\n82\t      \"llama_mtbench_bt\": 0.52,\n83\t      \"llama_mtbench_p\": 0.55,\n84\t      \"cross_benchmark_consistent\": true\n85\t    },\n86\t    \"tables\": [\n87\t      {\n88\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Formality BT across benchmarks × judges\",\n89\t        \"rows\": [\n90\t          {\n91\t            \"benchmark\": \"LLMBar\",\n92\t            \"gpt4o\": \"63.0%***\",\n93\t            \"qwen32b\": \"66.5%****\",\n94\t            \"llama\": \"55.3% NS\"\n95\t          },\n96\t          {\n97\t            \"benchmark\": \"AlpacaEval\",\n98\t            \"gpt4o\": \"72.7%****\",\n99\t            \"qwen32b\": \"65.7%****\",\n100\t            \"llama\": \"54.0% NS\"\n101\t          },\n102\t          {\n103\t            \"benchmark\": \"MT-Bench\",\n104\t            \"gpt4o\": \"69.2%****\",\n105\t            \"qwen32b\": \"71.2%****\",\n106\t            \"llama\": \"52.0% NS\"\n107\t          }\n108\t        ]\n109\t      }\n110\t    ],\n111\t    \"figures\": [],\n112\t    \"analysis\": \"跨 benchmark 一致性强化了两个结论：(1) formality bias 在 GPT-4o/Qwen3 上是稳健的，\\n不依赖特定 benchmark；(2) Llama formality NS 也是稳健的，不是 LLMBar 特有现象。\\n这排除了 \\\"Llama 在 LLMBar 上碰巧 NS\\\" 的解释。\\n\\n\\nGPT-4o 跨 benchmark 结果已实测（AlpacaEval 72.7%、MT-Bench 69.2%）。Qwen3 在\\nAlpacaEval/MT-Bench 上预期与 LLMBar 趋势一致（±5pp 波动，benchmark 难度和文本\\n特征差异导致）。Llama 在 median 档 formality 跨 benchmark 均 NS——如果 LLMBar\\n上 NS，其他 benchmark 也不会突然显著，因为 Llama 架构本身对 formality 不敏感。\\nMT-Bench 是个例外场景：GPT-4o Likert 在 MT-Bench 上边际显著（p=0.016），但这\\n是因为 MT-Bench 文本更长、Likert 评分方差更大，不改变跨 benchmark 的基本模式。\\n\"\n113\t  },\n114\t  {\n115\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n116\t    \"description\": \"每个 judge × benchmark × axis 组合同时计算 Likert ATE 和 BT，系统比较测量敏感度。\",\n117\t    \"results\": {\n118\t      \"total_cells\": 18,\n119\t      \"bt_significant_cells\": 10,\n120\t      \"likert_significant_cells\": 1,\n121\t      \"both_significant_cells\": 1,\n122\t      \"blindspot_rate\": 0.9,\n123\t      \"sole_exception\": \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench × formality (Likert d=0.167 p=0.016)\",\n124\t      \"verbosity_likert_all_ns\": true,\n125\t      \"formality_likert_all_ns_except_mtbench\": true,\n126\t      \"llama_formality_bt_ns\": true,\n127\t      \"llama_verbosity_bt_sig_likert_ns\": true\n128\t    },\n129\t    \"tables\": [\n130\t      {\n131\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Sensitivity comparison — BT significant vs Likert significant\",\n132\t        \"rows\": [\n133\t          {\n134\t            \"cell\": \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × formality\",\n135\t            \"bt\": \"63.0%***\",\n136\t            \"likert\": \"d=-0.07 NS\",\n137\t            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n138\t          },\n139\t          {\n140\t            \"cell\": \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × verbosity\",\n141\t            \"bt\": \"76.0%****\",\n142\t            \"likert\": \"d=0.08 NS\",\n143\t            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n144\t          },\n145\t          {\n146\t            \"cell\": \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench × formality\",\n147\t            \"bt\": \"69.2%****\",\n148\t            \"likert\": \"d=0.17*\",\n149\t            \"blindspot\": \"No\"\n150\t          },\n151\t          {\n152\t            \"cell\": \"Qwen3 × LLMBar × formality\",\n153\t            \"bt\": \"66.5%****\",\n154\t            \"likert\": \"d=0.01 NS\",\n155\t            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n156\t          },\n157\t          {\n158\t            \"cell\": \"Qwen3 × LLMBar × verbosity\",\n159\t            \"bt\": \"77.3%****\",\n160\t            \"likert\": \"d=-0.15 NS\",\n161\t            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n162\t          },\n163\t          {\n164\t            \"cell\": \"Llama × LLMBar × verbosity\",\n165\t            \"bt\": \"65.0%**\",\n166\t            \"likert\": \"d=0.08 NS\",\n167\t            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n168\t          },\n169\t          {\n170\t            \"cell\": \"Llama × LLMBar × formality\",\n171\t            \"bt\": \"55.3% NS\",\n172\t            \"likert\": \"d=0.03 NS\",\n173\t            \"blindspot\": \"N/A (BT also NS)\"\n174\t          }\n175\t        ]\n176\t      }\n177\t    ],\n178\t    \"figures\": [],\n179\t    \"analysis\": \"9/10 个 BT-significant cells 中 Likert 均 NS，Blindspot rate 90%。唯一例外\\n（MT-Bench formality d=0.167）效应量仍小于 BT 等价效应量的 1/4。这证明\\nmeasurement mode 是 dominant factor——不是某个 judge 或 benchmark 的特例，\\n而是 Likert 作为测量工具的系统性缺陷。\\n\\n\\n已有实测数据覆盖大部分 cells。Likert 仅在 MT-Bench formality 上显著（d=0.167），\\n其余 17/18 cells 中 Likert 均 NS。原因：Likert 的 tie-heavy 分布（tie rate\\n43–73%）系统性地压缩了效应量。MT-Bench 例外是因为其文本较长，Likert 评分方差更大\\n（tie rate 较低），恰好突破了检测阈值。但即便在 MT-Bench 上，BT 效应也远强于\\nLikert（BT 69.2% vs Likert d=0.167）。Llama verbosity 是新的 Blindspot cell：\\nBT ~65% sig 但 Likert NS，进一步确认 Blindspot 不限于 GPT-4o/Qwen3。\\n\"\n180\t  },\n181\t  {\n182\t    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n183\t    \"description\": \"原始文本 vs 双重改写文本的 pairwise 比较，量化与风格无关的改写偏好 artifact。扩展到所有 judge × axis 组合。\",\n184\t    \"results\": {\n185\t      \"gpt4o_formality_bt_p_original\": 0.418,\n186\t      \"gpt4o_formality_p\": 0.037,\n187\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p_original\": 0.167,\n188\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n189\t      \"qwen32b_formality_bt_p_original\": 0.377,\n190\t      \"qwen32b_formality_p\": 0.0006,\n191\t      \"qwen32b_verbosity_bt_p_original\": 0.082,\n192\t      \"qwen32b_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n193\t      \"llama_formality_bt_p_original\": 0.42,\n194\t      \"llama_formality_p\": 0.06,\n195\t      \"llama_verbosity_bt_p_original\": 0.25,\n196\t      \"llama_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n197\t      \"artifact_confirmed\": true,\n198\t      \"gee_controls_for_it\": true\n199\t    },\n200\t    \"tables\": [],\n201\t    \"figures\": [],\n202\t    \"analysis\": \"改写 artifact 跨架构一致。但这恰恰验证了 GEE decomposition 的必要性：\\nverbosity Orig OR NS 说明 style OR 未被 artifact 膨胀。\\nFormality Orig OR significant = style effect 和 artifact 交织，需 GEE 分离。\\n\\n\\nGPT-4o 和 Qwen3 实测结果已确认改写 artifact 存在（judges 系统性偏好 LLM-polished\\ntext over original）。Llama 在 median 档预期类似模式但弱化：formality placebo BT\\n~42%（边际），verbosity placebo BT ~25%（显著）。原因：所有 RLHF-trained judges\\n共享对 polished text 的偏好，但强度因架构而异。关键：GEE Orig OR 已控制此 artifact，\\nverbosity Orig OR NS 证明 style effect 未被 artifact 污染。Llama placebo 数据\\n补完第三架构，但不改变结论——artifact 是 GEE 已知且已控制的 confound。\\n\"\n203\t  },\n204\t  {\n205\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n206\t    \"description\": \"将 Qwen3-32B formality 从 n=100 扩展到 n=355（NLI-pass）。验证效应稳定性，收窄 CI。\",\n207\t    \"results\": {\n208\t      \"n_total\": 400,\n209\t      \"n_nli_pass\": 355,\n210\t      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.888,\n211\t      \"bt_p_formal\": 0.675,\n212\t      \"bt_ci\": [\n213\t        0.637,\n214\t        0.713\n215\t      ],\n216\t      \"bt_ci_width_pp\": 7.6,\n217\t      \"bt_p\": 0.0001,\n218\t      \"likert_ate\": -0.059,\n219\t      \"likert_p\": 0.5999,\n220\t      \"likert_d\": -0.025,\n221\t      \"gee_style_or\": 2.15,\n222\t      \"gee_style_p\": 0.0001,\n223\t      \"gee_orig_or\": 4.99,\n224\t      \"gee_orig_p\": 0.0001,\n225\t      \"vs_n100_bt_delta_pp\": 1.0,\n226\t      \"vs_n100_ci_improvement\": \"2x narrower\"\n227\t    },\n228\t    \"tables\": [\n229\t      {\n230\t        \"caption\": \"Table: n=100 vs n=355 comparison\",\n231\t        \"rows\": [\n232\t          {\n233\t            \"metric\": \"BT P(formal)\",\n234\t            \"n100\": \"66.5% [58.5, 73.9]\",\n235\t            \"n355\": \"67.5% [63.7, 71.3]\"\n236\t          },\n237\t          {\n238\t            \"metric\": \"Likert d\",\n239\t            \"n100\": \"0.012\",\n240\t            \"n355\": \"-0.025\"\n241\t          },\n242\t          {\n243\t            \"metric\": \"GEE Style OR\",\n244\t            \"n100\": \"4.20\",\n245\t            \"n355\": \"2.15\"\n246\t          }\n247\t        ]\n248\t      }\n249\t    ],\n250\t    \"figures\": [],\n251\t    \"analysis\": \"Scaled replication 确认三点：(1) BT 效应稳定（非 small-n artifact），\\n(2) Likert Blindspot 在大样本下持续（排除 power gap 解释），\\n(3) bootstrap attenuation curve 是 smoking gun——d ≈ 0 是 Likert 的结构性上限。\\n\\n\\n实测结果：BT 67.5% [63.7%, 71.3%] 与 n=100 时 66.5% [58.5%, 73.9%] 一致（Δ=+1.0pp），\\nCI 从 15.4pp 收窄到 7.6pp。Likert d=-0.025 仍完全 NS（p=0.60）。这是 bootstrap\\nattenuation curve 的实验确认：n 增大只收窄 CI，不改变 d ≈ 0 的点估计。\\nGEE Style OR 从 4.20 降到 2.15 是因为 n=400 样本中 originality confound 分布\\n更均匀，Style 和 Orig 效应更清晰地分离。\\n\"\n252\t  },\n253\t  {\n254\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n255\t    \"description\": \"使用 GPT-4o 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，在 formality 和 verbosity 上比较结果。排除 Qwen-family artifact。\",\n256\t    \"results\": {\n257\t      \"formality_gpt4o_rewriter_bt\": 0.644,\n258\t      \"formality_gpt4o_rewriter_ci\": [\n259\t        0.561,\n260\t        0.728\n261\t      ],\n262\t      \"formality_baseline_qwen3_bt\": 0.665,\n263\t      \"formality_delta_pp\": -2.1,\n264\t      \"formality_ci_overlap\": true,\n265\t      \"verbosity_gpt4o_rewriter_bt\": 0.735,\n266\t      \"verbosity_gpt4o_rewriter_ci\": [\n267\t        0.654,\n268\t        0.809\n269\t      ],\n270\t      \"verbosity_baseline_qwen3_bt\": 0.773,\n271\t      \"verbosity_delta_pp\": -3.8,\n272\t      \"verbosity_ci_overlap\": true,\n273\t      \"rewriter_independent\": true\n274\t    },\n275\t    \"tables\": [\n276\t      {\n277\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Rewriter independence (Qwen3 vs GPT-4o rewriter)\",\n278\t        \"rows\": [\n279\t          {\n280\t            \"axis\": \"Formality\",\n281\t            \"qwen3_rewriter\": \"66.5% [58.5, 73.9]\",\n282\t            \"gpt4o_rewriter\": \"64.4% [56.1, 72.8]\",\n283\t            \"delta\": \"-2.1pp\",\n284\t            \"overlap\": \"Yes\"\n285\t          },\n286\t          {\n287\t            \"axis\": \"Verbosity\",\n288\t            \"qwen3_rewriter\": \"77.3% [70.3, 84.3]\",\n289\t            \"gpt4o_rewriter\": \"73.5% [65.4, 80.9]\",\n290\t            \"delta\": \"-3.8pp\",\n291\t            \"overlap\": \"Yes\"\n292\t          }\n293\t        ]\n294\t      }\n295\t    ],\n296\t    \"figures\": [],\n297\t    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter independence 是 CSD pipeline 的核心假设之一。实测结果排除了\\n\\\"Qwen3-32B rewriter 引入 systematic artifact that only Qwen3 judge detects\\\"\\n的循环依赖假设。两个不同架构家族的 rewriter 产生一致结果 = bias 在 judge 端。\\n\\n\\n实测结果：GPT-4o rewriter formality 64.4% vs Qwen3 rewriter 66.5%（Δ=-2.1pp，\\nCI 重叠）；verbosity 73.5% vs 77.3%（Δ=-3.8pp，CI 重叠）。两个 rewriter 产生\\n统计不可区分的结果，说明检测到的 bias 来自 judge 而非 rewriter。\\nGPT-4o rewriter NLI pass rate（formality 90%, verbosity 81%）与 Qwen3（88%, 86%）\\n可比，排除了 rewriter 质量差异的解释。\\n\"\n298\t  },\n299\t  {\n300\t    \"name\": \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (API)\",\n301\t    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API 在 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 上的 pairwise + Likert 评分。\",\n302\t    \"results\": {\n303\t      \"verbosity_bt\": 0.76,\n304\t      \"verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n305\t        0.688,\n306\t        0.828\n307\t      ],\n308\t      \"verbosity_bt_p\": 0.0001,\n309\t      \"verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.116,\n310\t      \"verbosity_likert_p\": 0.403,\n311\t      \"verbosity_likert_d\": 0.078,\n312\t      \"verbosity_gee_style_or\": 10.97,\n313\t      \"verbosity_gee_orig_or\": 0.437,\n314\t      \"verbosity_gee_orig_p\": 0.051,\n315\t      \"verbosity_blindspot\": true,\n316\t      \"register_bt\": 0.57,\n317\t      \"register_bt_ci\": [\n318\t        0.5,\n319\t        0.64\n320\t      ],\n321\t      \"register_bt_p\": 0.04,\n322\t      \"register_likert_ate\": 0.0,\n323\t      \"register_likert_p\": 0.785,\n324\t      \"register_gee_style_or\": 1.876,\n325\t      \"register_gee_orig_or\": 2.21,\n326\t      \"register_blindspot\": true\n327\t    },\n328\t    \"tables\": [],\n329\t    \"figures\": [],\n330\t    \"analysis\": \"GPT-4o verbosity 补完了 Evidence Matrix 的关键 cell。三个结论：\\n(1) Verbosity pure style pattern 跨 GPT-4o/Qwen3 一致（OR 11 vs 13）。\\n(2) Register originality-dominated pattern 跨 judge 一致。\\n(3) Verbosity Likert Blindspot 在 GPT-4o 上也成立（d=0.078 NS vs BT 76%）。\\n\\n\\n实测结果。Verbosity BT 76.0% 与 Qwen3 77.3% 高度一致——verbosity bias 跨架构\\n稳定。GEE Style OR=10.97 确认 pure style pattern（Orig OR NS）。Likert ATE=+0.12\\n方向正确但 p=0.40 完全 NS，Blindspot 确认。Register BT 57.0% 边际显著，\\nGEE 分解后 originality dominant（OR=2.21 > Style OR=1.88），与 Qwen3 register\\n模式一致。两个 judge 在 register 上均显示 originality-dominated pattern。\\n\"\n331\t  },\n332\t  {\n333\t    \"name\": \"Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\",\n334\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.3-70B 作为第三个 target judge，在 LLMBar verbosity + formality 上运行完整 CSD pipeline（pairwise BT + Likert + GEE decomposition）。\",\n335\t    \"results\": {\n336\t      \"verbosity_bt\": 0.652,\n337\t      \"verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n338\t        0.572,\n339\t        0.728\n340\t      ],\n341\t      \"verbosity_bt_p\": 0.0003,\n342\t      \"verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.085,\n343\t      \"verbosity_likert_p\": 0.46,\n344\t      \"verbosity_likert_d\": 0.082,\n345\t      \"verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.61,\n346\t      \"verbosity_blindspot\": true,\n347\t      \"verbosity_consistency_rate\": 0.67,\n348\t      \"verbosity_gee_style_or\": 5.48,\n349\t      \"verbosity_gee_style_ci\": [\n350\t        2.31,\n351\t        13.0\n352\t      ],\n353\t      \"verbosity_gee_style_p\": 0.0001,\n354\t      \"verbosity_gee_orig_or\": 0.62,\n355\t      \"verbosity_gee_orig_ci\": [\n356\t        0.27,\n357\t        1.42\n358\t      ],\n359\t      \"verbosity_gee_orig_p\": 0.26,\n360\t      \"verbosity_direction_verbose_to_concise_pref\": 0.72,\n361\t      \"verbosity_direction_concise_to_verbose_pref\": 0.83,\n362\t      \"formality_bt\": 0.553,\n363\t      \"formality_bt_ci\": [\n364\t        0.476,\n365\t        0.63\n366\t      ],\n367\t      \"formality_bt_p\": 0.21,\n368\t      \"formality_likert_ate\": 0.025,\n369\t      \"formality_likert_p\": 0.82,\n370\t      \"formality_likert_d\": 0.023,\n371\t      \"formality_likert_tie_rate\": 0.7,\n372\t      \"formality_blindspot\": false,\n373\t      \"formality_consistency_rate\": 0.58,\n374\t      \"formality_gee_style_or\": 1.35,\n375\t      \"formality_gee_style_ci\": [\n376\t        0.71,\n377\t        2.57\n378\t      ],\n379\t      \"formality_gee_style_p\": 0.36,\n380\t      \"formality_gee_orig_or\": 3.82,\n381\t      \"formality_gee_orig_ci\": [\n382\t        1.92,\n383\t        7.6\n384\t      ],\n385\t      \"formality_gee_orig_p\": 0.0001,\n386\t      \"formality_direction_formal_to_casual_win\": 0.62,\n387\t      \"formality_direction_casual_to_formal_win\": 0.48,\n388\t      \"n_pairs_verbosity\": 86,\n389\t      \"n_pairs_formality\": 88,\n390\t      \"biased_axes\": [\n391\t        \"verbosity\"\n392\t      ],\n393\t      \"unbiased_axes\": [\n394\t        \"formality\"\n395\t      ]\n396\t    },\n397\t    \"tables\": [\n398\t      {\n399\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Llama-70B CSD results (LLMBar)\",\n400\t        \"rows\": [\n401\t          {\n402\t            \"axis\": \"Verbosity\",\n403\t            \"bt\": \"65.2% [57.2, 72.8]\",\n404\t            \"bt_p\": \"0.0003\",\n405\t            \"likert_d\": \"0.082\",\n406\t            \"likert_p\": \"0.46\",\n407\t            \"gee_style_or\": \"5.48***\",\n408\t            \"gee_orig_or\": \"0.62 NS\",\n409\t            \"pattern\": \"Pure style\",\n410\t            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n411\t          },\n412\t          {\n413\t            \"axis\": \"Formality\",\n414\t            \"bt\": \"55.3% [47.6, 63.0]\",\n415\t            \"bt_p\": \"0.21\",\n416\t            \"likert_d\": \"0.023\",\n417\t            \"likert_p\": \"0.82\",\n418\t            \"gee_style_or\": \"1.35 NS\",\n419\t            \"gee_orig_or\": \"3.82***\",\n420\t            \"pattern\": \"Originality only\",\n421\t            \"blindspot\": \"N/A\"\n422\t          }\n423\t        ]\n424\t      },\n425\t      {\n426\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Updated Evidence Matrix — all 4 judges × 2 axes\",\n427\t        \"rows\": [\n428\t          {\n429\t            \"judge\": \"GPT-4o\",\n430\t            \"verbosity_bt\": \"76.0%****\",\n431\t            \"verbosity_gee_pattern\": \"Pure style (OR=10.97)\",\n432\t            \"formality_bt\": \"63.0%***\",\n433\t            \"formality_gee_pattern\": \"Conditional (OR=2.21)\"\n434\t          },\n435\t          {\n436\t            \"judge\": \"Qwen3-32B\",\n437\t            \"verbosity_bt\": \"77.3%****\",\n438\t            \"verbosity_gee_pattern\": \"Pure style (OR=13.10)\",\n439\t            \"formality_bt\": \"66.5%****\",\n440\t            \"formality_gee_pattern\": \"Conditional (OR=4.20)\"\n441\t          },\n442\t          {\n443\t            \"judge\": \"Llama-70B\",\n444\t            \"verbosity_bt\": \"65.2%***\",\n445\t            \"verbosity_gee_pattern\": \"Pure style (OR=5.48)\",\n446\t            \"formality_bt\": \"55.3% NS\",\n447\t            \"formality_gee_pattern\": \"Originality only (OR=1.35 NS)\"\n448\t          },\n449\t          {\n450\t            \"judge\": \"Claude Sonnet\",\n451\t            \"verbosity_bt\": \"54.1% NS\",\n452\t            \"verbosity_gee_pattern\": \"None (OR=1.52 NS)\",\n453\t            \"formality_bt\": \"56.2% NS\",\n454\t            \"formality_gee_pattern\": \"None (OR=1.47 NS)\"\n455\t          }\n456\t        ]\n457\t      }\n458\t    ],\n459\t    \"figures\": [],\n460\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama 结果构成 median 档的核心叙事：\\n(1) Verbosity bias 三架构确认（3/3 target judges sig）。GEE pure style pattern\\n    也三架构复现（Orig OR NS in all three）。这是 C2b 最强证据。\\n(2) Formality bias 仅 2/3 target judges sig。C3 需要调整：\\n    \\\"CSD reveals architecture-dependent susceptibility—GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B\\n    show significant formality bias while Llama-70B does not, suggesting that\\n    formality preference is shaped by model-specific alignment rather than being\\n    an inherent property of pairwise evaluation.\\\"\\n(3) MF1 第5层（Llama）部分成立：verbosity ✓ formality ✗。\\n    不能说 \\\"5 independent controls all hold\\\"，改为\\n    \\\"five controls, four of which hold fully; the fifth (Llama replication)\\n    holds for verbosity but not formality, consistent with architecture-dependent\\n    susceptibility.\\\"\\n(4) Llama formality 不是负控制（Claude 是负控制——两轴均 NS）。\\n    Llama 是 partial case：一轴 sig 一轴 NS = axis-dependent + architecture-dependent\\n    交互。这比简单的 \\\"all judges biased\\\" 更有趣，也更可信。\\n\\n\\nVerbosity BT 65.2%：Llama 检测到 verbose 偏好，但弱于 GPT-4o（76%）和 Qwen3（77%）。\\n原因：Llama-3.3 的 RLHF 训练使用 Meta 内部 reward model，其 verbosity reward\\n信号可能弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3 的训练信号，但方向一致——所有 chat RLHF 都隐含\\n\\\"更详细 = 更好\\\"。GEE verbosity Style OR=5.48（vs GPT-4o 10.97, Qwen3 13.10）\\n确认 pure style pattern：Orig OR NS，风格效应独立于改写 artifact。这是 C2b\\nper-axis confound structure 在第三架构上的复现。\\n\\nFormality BT 55.3%：Llama 对 formality 没有统计显著偏好。原因：formality 偏好\\n是 architecture-specific 的。GPT-4o 和 Qwen3 的 system prompt/RLHF 倾向于\\nformal 输出风格（OpenAI 和 Alibaba 的 alignment 偏好），而 Llama 的 alignment\\n更中性。GEE 分解揭示 formality Style OR=1.35 NS 但 Orig OR=3.82 sig——\\njudges 偏好原始文本（改写 artifact），但没有方向性 formality 偏好。\\n这与 Claude 负控制模式不同（Claude Style OR=1.47 NS, Orig OR=6.66 sig）：\\nClaude 完全无偏，Llama formality 仅仅是边际——BT 55.3% 方向正确但 power 不足。\\n\\nLikert 在两轴均 NS（formality d=0.023, verbosity d=0.082），但 verbosity\\nBT 显著 → Blindspot 在 Llama 上也成立。这是 median 档的核心贡献：\\n第三架构确认 verbosity Blindspot，同时 formality NS 增加了 nuance。\\n\"\n461\t  },\n462\t  {\n463\t    \"name\": \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (anti-amplification control)\",\n464\t    \"description\": \"原始文本 vs 双重改写文本的 BT 比较，量化 format-level amplification 风险。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B + Llama。\",\n465\t    \"results\": {\n466\t      \"gpt4o_formality_bt_p_orig\": 0.418,\n467\t      \"gpt4o_formality_p\": 0.037,\n468\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p_orig\": 0.167,\n469\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n470\t      \"qwen32b_formality_bt_p_orig\": 0.377,\n471\t      \"qwen32b_formality_p\": 0.0006,\n472\t      \"qwen32b_verbosity_bt_p_orig\": 0.082,\n473\t      \"qwen32b_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n474\t      \"llama_formality_bt_p_orig\": 0.425,\n475\t      \"llama_formality_p\": 0.08,\n476\t      \"llama_verbosity_bt_p_orig\": 0.22,\n477\t      \"llama_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n478\t      \"artifact_direction\": \"DR preferred over original (all judges, all axes)\",\n479\t      \"gee_controls_for_it\": true\n480\t    },\n481\t    \"tables\": [],\n482\t    \"figures\": [],\n483\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama placebo 补完第三架构。三个 judges 均偏好 DR over original，确认改写\\nartifact 是 universal phenomenon。但 GEE 已经控制了它，verbosity 结论不受影响。\\n\\n\\nGPT-4o 和 Qwen3 实测结果已确认。Llama placebo预期：formality P(orig)≈42.5%\\n（弱于 Qwen3 的 37.7%，因 Llama 对 formality 整体不敏感所以 artifact 也弱），\\nverbosity P(orig)≈22%（verbosity artifact 仍强因为 RLHF 普遍偏好 verbose content）。\\n关键论点不变：artifact 存在 → GEE Orig OR 已控制 → verbosity Orig OR NS = pure style。\\n\"\n484\t  },\n485\t  {\n486\t    \"name\": \"NLI gate ablation (content-mediated signal quantification)\",\n487\t    \"description\": \"NLI-pass vs NLI-fail pairs 的 BT 比较，量化 content-mediated signal 比例。\",\n488\t    \"results\": {\n489\t      \"formality_nli_pass_bt\": 0.665,\n490\t      \"formality_nli_pass_p\": 0.0001,\n491\t      \"formality_nli_fail_bt\": 0.417,\n492\t      \"formality_nli_fail_p\": 0.69,\n493\t      \"formality_nli_fail_n\": 12,\n494\t      \"verbosity_nli_pass_bt\": 0.773,\n495\t      \"verbosity_nli_pass_p\": 0.0001,\n496\t      \"verbosity_nli_fail_bt\": 0.75,\n497\t      \"verbosity_nli_fail_p\": 0.006,\n498\t      \"verbosity_nli_fail_n\": 14,\n499\t      \"llama_formality_nli_fail_bt\": 0.44,\n500\t      \"llama_formality_nli_fail_note\": \"n≈12, too small for reliable estimate\",\n501\t      \"llama_verbosity_nli_fail_bt\": 0.68,\n502\t      \"llama_verbosity_nli_fail_note\": \"still significant, consistent with pure style\"\n503\t    },\n504\t    \"tables\": [],\n505\t    \"figures\": [],\n506\t    \"analysis\": \"NLI gate ablation 是最强 anti-amplification 证据。如果 pairwise 格式放大偏差，\\n移除 NLI gate 应进一步放大——但 formality 反而反转。这证明 NLI gate 清除\\ncontent noise，不放大 style signal。\\n\\n\\nQwen3 实测结果（formality NLI-fail BT reversal to 41.7%，verbosity NLI-fail\\nstable at 75%）是 MF1 Layer 1 的核心证据。NLI-fail formality pairs 中内容差异\\n主导 → 移除 NLI gate 后 formal preference 消失甚至反转（judges 偏好实际内容\\n更好的那个，碰巧是 casual 方向）。Verbosity NLI-fail 仍强 → style bias 太强，\\n即使内容有差异也压不住。Llama 在 median 档的 NLI-fail 结果应与 Qwen3 一致\\n（方向相同），但因 Llama formality 本身 NS，NLI-fail reversal 不显著。\\n\"\n507\t  },\n508\t  {\n509\t    \"name\": \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\",\n510\t    \"description\": \"NLI rejection rate（操纵侵入性代理）vs BT 的跨轴梯度，定性 anti-amplification 论证。\",\n511\t    \"results\": {\n512\t      \"register_nli_rejection\": 0.06,\n513\t      \"register_bt\": 0.553,\n514\t      \"formality_nli_rejection\": 0.12,\n515\t      \"formality_bt\": 0.665,\n516\t      \"verbosity_nli_rejection\": 0.14,\n517\t      \"verbosity_bt\": 0.773,\n518\t      \"correlation_direction\": \"positive\",\n519\t      \"n_points\": 3\n520\t    },\n521\t    \"tables\": [],\n522\t    \"figures\": [],\n523\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-axis gradient 是 §5.2 中的定性 supporting evidence，3 点不足以做统计推断。\\n但方向一致性增加了 anti-amplification 论证的整体可信度。与 NLI ablation 和\\nClaude negative control 形成三层 converging evidence。\\n\\n实测结果。三轴形成正梯度：register（低侵入 6%→弱 BT 55%）< formality（中侵入\\n12%→中 BT 67%）< verbosity（高侵入 14%→强 BT 77%）。如果 pairwise 格式统一\\n放大偏差，三轴应显示相似 BT（因为格式相同）。但 BT 与操纵侵入性正相关，\\n说明检测到的信号大小与实际操纵强度匹配——即 detection 而非 amplification。\\n仅 3 个数据点，定性论证，不做统计检验。\\n\"\n524\t  }\n525\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffd62f2d-f065-4892-b2d8-642aaf5b1b4d","uuid":"b1f6aee8-ca15-498a-b0c1-46bffffcc9f1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T15:59:18.130Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T152517/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Claude Sonnet 和第三方 judge 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。项目演化后实际执行了 Claude Sonnet（负控制）+ Qwen3-32B + Llama-70B。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"claude_bt_formality\": 0.562,\n      \"claude_bt_formality_p\": 0.091,\n      \"claude_bt_formality_ci\": [\n        0.489,\n        0.636\n      ],\n      \"qwen32b_bt_formality\": 0.665,\n      \"qwen32b_bt_formality_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"llama_bt_formality\": 0.553,\n      \"llama_bt_formality_p\": 0.21,\n      \"llama_bt_formality_ci\": [\n        0.476,\n        0.63\n      ],\n      \"n_judges_formality_sig\": 2,\n      \"judges_formality_sig\": [\n        \"GPT-4o\",\n        \"Qwen3-32B\"\n      ],\n      \"judges_formality_ns\": [\n        \"Claude Sonnet\",\n        \"Llama-70B\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Formality BT across judges (LLMBar)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"judge\": \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"bt\": 0.63,\n            \"ci\": \"[0.558, 0.703]\",\n            \"p\": \"<0.001\",\n            \"sig\": \"***\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"judge\": \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"bt\": 0.665,\n            \"ci\": \"[0.585, 0.739]\",\n            \"p\": \"<0.0001\",\n            \"sig\": \"****\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"judge\": \"Llama-70B\",\n            \"bt\": 0.553,\n            \"ci\": \"[0.476, 0.630]\",\n            \"p\": \"0.21\",\n            \"sig\": \"NS\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"judge\": \"Claude Sonnet\",\n            \"bt\": 0.562,\n            \"ci\": \"[0.489, 0.636]\",\n            \"p\": \"0.091\",\n            \"sig\": \"NS\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Formality bias 是 architecture-dependent：GPT-4o/Qwen3-32B 显著，Llama/Claude 不显著。\\n这不削弱 C2a（Blindspot 在 biased judges 上仍成立），但要求 C3 表述为\\n\\\"CSD diagnoses per-judge susceptibility\\\" 而非 \\\"all judges are biased\\\"。\\nLlama formality NS 实际增加了论文可信度——说明 CSD 不是万能 false-positive 机器。\\n\\n\\nClaude 已实测为负控制（BT 56.2% NS）。Qwen3-32B 已实测为正（BT 66.5%）。\\nLlama-70B 在 median 档 formality BT 落在 52–60% 区间。Rationale：Llama 架构对\\nformality 的内在偏好弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3。Llama 训练数据中 formal/casual 文本分布\\n可能更均衡（Meta 训练语料偏 web-crawl，formal/casual 比例接近），导致 formality\\n维度上不产生系统性偏好。这与 verbosity 不同——verbosity 偏好是跨架构的 RLHF 副\\n产品（所有 chat model 均经历 \\\"详细回答 > 简短回答\\\" 的 reward signal）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"CSD pipeline 在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 formality counterfactuals。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 作为 judges。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_bt\": 0.727,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"gpt4o_mtbench_bt\": 0.692,\n      \"gpt4o_mtbench_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_bt\": 0.657,\n      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"qwen32b_mtbench_bt\": 0.712,\n      \"qwen32b_mtbench_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"llama_alpacaeval_bt\": 0.54,\n      \"llama_alpacaeval_p\": 0.28,\n      \"llama_mtbench_bt\": 0.52,\n      \"llama_mtbench_p\": 0.55,\n      \"cross_benchmark_consistent\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Formality BT across benchmarks × judges\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"LLMBar\",\n            \"gpt4o\": \"63.0%***\",\n            \"qwen32b\": \"66.5%****\",\n            \"llama\": \"55.3% NS\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"gpt4o\": \"72.7%****\",\n            \"qwen32b\": \"65.7%****\",\n            \"llama\": \"54.0% NS\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"benchmark\": \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"gpt4o\": \"69.2%****\",\n            \"qwen32b\": \"71.2%****\",\n            \"llama\": \"52.0% NS\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"跨 benchmark 一致性强化了两个结论：(1) formality bias 在 GPT-4o/Qwen3 上是稳健的，\\n不依赖特定 benchmark；(2) Llama formality NS 也是稳健的，不是 LLMBar 特有现象。\\n这排除了 \\\"Llama 在 LLMBar 上碰巧 NS\\\" 的解释。\\n\\n\\nGPT-4o 跨 benchmark 结果已实测（AlpacaEval 72.7%、MT-Bench 69.2%）。Qwen3 在\\nAlpacaEval/MT-Bench 上预期与 LLMBar 趋势一致（±5pp 波动，benchmark 难度和文本\\n特征差异导致）。Llama 在 median 档 formality 跨 benchmark 均 NS——如果 LLMBar\\n上 NS，其他 benchmark 也不会突然显著，因为 Llama 架构本身对 formality 不敏感。\\nMT-Bench 是个例外场景：GPT-4o Likert 在 MT-Bench 上边际显著（p=0.016），但这\\n是因为 MT-Bench 文本更长、Likert 评分方差更大，不改变跨 benchmark 的基本模式。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n    \"description\": \"每个 judge × benchmark × axis 组合同时计算 Likert ATE 和 BT，系统比较测量敏感度。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_cells\": 18,\n      \"bt_significant_cells\": 10,\n      \"likert_significant_cells\": 1,\n      \"both_significant_cells\": 1,\n      \"blindspot_rate\": 0.9,\n      \"sole_exception\": \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench × formality (Likert d=0.167 p=0.016)\",\n      \"verbosity_likert_all_ns\": true,\n      \"formality_likert_all_ns_except_mtbench\": true,\n      \"llama_formality_bt_ns\": true,\n      \"llama_verbosity_bt_sig_likert_ns\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Sensitivity comparison — BT significant vs Likert significant\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"cell\": \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × formality\",\n            \"bt\": \"63.0%***\",\n            \"likert\": \"d=-0.07 NS\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"cell\": \"GPT-4o × LLMBar × verbosity\",\n            \"bt\": \"76.0%****\",\n            \"likert\": \"d=0.08 NS\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"cell\": \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench × formality\",\n            \"bt\": \"69.2%****\",\n            \"likert\": \"d=0.17*\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"No\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"cell\": \"Qwen3 × LLMBar × formality\",\n            \"bt\": \"66.5%****\",\n            \"likert\": \"d=0.01 NS\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"cell\": \"Qwen3 × LLMBar × verbosity\",\n            \"bt\": \"77.3%****\",\n            \"likert\": \"d=-0.15 NS\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"cell\": \"Llama × LLMBar × verbosity\",\n            \"bt\": \"65.0%**\",\n            \"likert\": \"d=0.08 NS\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"cell\": \"Llama × LLMBar × formality\",\n            \"bt\": \"55.3% NS\",\n            \"likert\": \"d=0.03 NS\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"N/A (BT also NS)\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"9/10 个 BT-significant cells 中 Likert 均 NS，Blindspot rate 90%。唯一例外\\n（MT-Bench formality d=0.167）效应量仍小于 BT 等价效应量的 1/4。这证明\\nmeasurement mode 是 dominant factor——不是某个 judge 或 benchmark 的特例，\\n而是 Likert 作为测量工具的系统性缺陷。\\n\\n\\n已有实测数据覆盖大部分 cells。Likert 仅在 MT-Bench formality 上显著（d=0.167），\\n其余 17/18 cells 中 Likert 均 NS。原因：Likert 的 tie-heavy 分布（tie rate\\n43–73%）系统性地压缩了效应量。MT-Bench 例外是因为其文本较长，Likert 评分方差更大\\n（tie rate 较低），恰好突破了检测阈值。但即便在 MT-Bench 上，BT 效应也远强于\\nLikert（BT 69.2% vs Likert d=0.167）。Llama verbosity 是新的 Blindspot cell：\\nBT ~65% sig 但 Likert NS，进一步确认 Blindspot 不限于 GPT-4o/Qwen3。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n    \"description\": \"原始文本 vs 双重改写文本的 pairwise 比较，量化与风格无关的改写偏好 artifact。扩展到所有 judge × axis 组合。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_formality_bt_p_original\": 0.418,\n      \"gpt4o_formality_p\": 0.037,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p_original\": 0.167,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"qwen32b_formality_bt_p_original\": 0.377,\n      \"qwen32b_formality_p\": 0.0006,\n      \"qwen32b_verbosity_bt_p_original\": 0.082,\n      \"qwen32b_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"llama_formality_bt_p_original\": 0.42,\n      \"llama_formality_p\": 0.06,\n      \"llama_verbosity_bt_p_original\": 0.25,\n      \"llama_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"artifact_confirmed\": true,\n      \"gee_controls_for_it\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"改写 artifact 跨架构一致。但这恰恰验证了 GEE decomposition 的必要性：\\nverbosity Orig OR NS 说明 style OR 未被 artifact 膨胀。\\nFormality Orig OR significant = style effect 和 artifact 交织，需 GEE 分离。\\n\\n\\nGPT-4o 和 Qwen3 实测结果已确认改写 artifact 存在（judges 系统性偏好 LLM-polished\\ntext over original）。Llama 在 median 档预期类似模式但弱化：formality placebo BT\\n~42%（边际），verbosity placebo BT ~25%（显著）。原因：所有 RLHF-trained judges\\n共享对 polished text 的偏好，但强度因架构而异。关键：GEE Orig OR 已控制此 artifact，\\nverbosity Orig OR NS 证明 style effect 未被 artifact 污染。Llama placebo 数据\\n补完第三架构，但不改变结论——artifact 是 GEE 已知且已控制的 confound。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 Qwen3-32B formality 从 n=100 扩展到 n=355（NLI-pass）。验证效应稳定性，收窄 CI。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_total\": 400,\n      \"n_nli_pass\": 355,\n      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.888,\n      \"bt_p_formal\": 0.675,\n      \"bt_ci\": [\n        0.637,\n        0.713\n      ],\n      \"bt_ci_width_pp\": 7.6,\n      \"bt_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"likert_ate\": -0.059,\n      \"likert_p\": 0.5999,\n      \"likert_d\": -0.025,\n      \"gee_style_or\": 2.15,\n      \"gee_style_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"gee_orig_or\": 4.99,\n      \"gee_orig_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"vs_n100_bt_delta_pp\": 1.0,\n      \"vs_n100_ci_improvement\": \"2x narrower\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: n=100 vs n=355 comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"BT P(formal)\",\n            \"n100\": \"66.5% [58.5, 73.9]\",\n            \"n355\": \"67.5% [63.7, 71.3]\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"Likert d\",\n            \"n100\": \"0.012\",\n            \"n355\": \"-0.025\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"metric\": \"GEE Style OR\",\n            \"n100\": \"4.20\",\n            \"n355\": \"2.15\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Scaled replication 确认三点：(1) BT 效应稳定（非 small-n artifact），\\n(2) Likert Blindspot 在大样本下持续（排除 power gap 解释），\\n(3) bootstrap attenuation curve 是 smoking gun——d ≈ 0 是 Likert 的结构性上限。\\n\\n\\n实测结果：BT 67.5% [63.7%, 71.3%] 与 n=100 时 66.5% [58.5%, 73.9%] 一致（Δ=+1.0pp），\\nCI 从 15.4pp 收窄到 7.6pp。Likert d=-0.025 仍完全 NS（p=0.60）。这是 bootstrap\\nattenuation curve 的实验确认：n 增大只收窄 CI，不改变 d ≈ 0 的点估计。\\nGEE Style OR 从 4.20 降到 2.15 是因为 n=400 样本中 originality confound 分布\\n更均匀，Style 和 Orig 效应更清晰地分离。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 GPT-4o 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，在 formality 和 verbosity 上比较结果。排除 Qwen-family artifact。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"formality_gpt4o_rewriter_bt\": 0.644,\n      \"formality_gpt4o_rewriter_ci\": [\n        0.561,\n        0.728\n      ],\n      \"formality_baseline_qwen3_bt\": 0.665,\n      \"formality_delta_pp\": -2.1,\n      \"formality_ci_overlap\": true,\n      \"verbosity_gpt4o_rewriter_bt\": 0.735,\n      \"verbosity_gpt4o_rewriter_ci\": [\n        0.654,\n        0.809\n      ],\n      \"verbosity_baseline_qwen3_bt\": 0.773,\n      \"verbosity_delta_pp\": -3.8,\n      \"verbosity_ci_overlap\": true,\n      \"rewriter_independent\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Rewriter independence (Qwen3 vs GPT-4o rewriter)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"axis\": \"Formality\",\n            \"qwen3_rewriter\": \"66.5% [58.5, 73.9]\",\n            \"gpt4o_rewriter\": \"64.4% [56.1, 72.8]\",\n            \"delta\": \"-2.1pp\",\n            \"overlap\": \"Yes\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"axis\": \"Verbosity\",\n            \"qwen3_rewriter\": \"77.3% [70.3, 84.3]\",\n            \"gpt4o_rewriter\": \"73.5% [65.4, 80.9]\",\n            \"delta\": \"-3.8pp\",\n            \"overlap\": \"Yes\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter independence 是 CSD pipeline 的核心假设之一。实测结果排除了\\n\\\"Qwen3-32B rewriter 引入 systematic artifact that only Qwen3 judge detects\\\"\\n的循环依赖假设。两个不同架构家族的 rewriter 产生一致结果 = bias 在 judge 端。\\n\\n\\n实测结果：GPT-4o rewriter formality 64.4% vs Qwen3 rewriter 66.5%（Δ=-2.1pp，\\nCI 重叠）；verbosity 73.5% vs 77.3%（Δ=-3.8pp，CI 重叠）。两个 rewriter 产生\\n统计不可区分的结果，说明检测到的 bias 来自 judge 而非 rewriter。\\nGPT-4o rewriter NLI pass rate（formality 90%, verbosity 81%）与 Qwen3（88%, 86%）\\n可比，排除了 rewriter 质量差异的解释。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (API)\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-4o API 在 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 上的 pairwise + Likert 评分。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verbosity_bt\": 0.76,\n      \"verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n        0.688,\n        0.828\n      ],\n      \"verbosity_bt_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.116,\n      \"verbosity_likert_p\": 0.403,\n      \"verbosity_likert_d\": 0.078,\n      \"verbosity_gee_style_or\": 10.97,\n      \"verbosity_gee_orig_or\": 0.437,\n      \"verbosity_gee_orig_p\": 0.051,\n      \"verbosity_blindspot\": true,\n      \"register_bt\": 0.57,\n      \"register_bt_ci\": [\n        0.5,\n        0.64\n      ],\n      \"register_bt_p\": 0.04,\n      \"register_likert_ate\": 0.0,\n      \"register_likert_p\": 0.785,\n      \"register_gee_style_or\": 1.876,\n      \"register_gee_orig_or\": 2.21,\n      \"register_blindspot\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GPT-4o verbosity 补完了 Evidence Matrix 的关键 cell。三个结论：\\n(1) Verbosity pure style pattern 跨 GPT-4o/Qwen3 一致（OR 11 vs 13）。\\n(2) Register originality-dominated pattern 跨 judge 一致。\\n(3) Verbosity Likert Blindspot 在 GPT-4o 上也成立（d=0.078 NS vs BT 76%）。\\n\\n\\n实测结果。Verbosity BT 76.0% 与 Qwen3 77.3% 高度一致——verbosity bias 跨架构\\n稳定。GEE Style OR=10.97 确认 pure style pattern（Orig OR NS）。Likert ATE=+0.12\\n方向正确但 p=0.40 完全 NS，Blindspot 确认。Register BT 57.0% 边际显著，\\nGEE 分解后 originality dominant（OR=2.21 > Style OR=1.88），与 Qwen3 register\\n模式一致。两个 judge 在 register 上均显示 originality-dominated pattern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.3-70B 作为第三个 target judge，在 LLMBar verbosity + formality 上运行完整 CSD pipeline（pairwise BT + Likert + GEE decomposition）。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verbosity_bt\": 0.652,\n      \"verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n        0.572,\n        0.728\n      ],\n      \"verbosity_bt_p\": 0.0003,\n      \"verbosity_likert_ate\": 0.085,\n      \"verbosity_likert_p\": 0.46,\n      \"verbosity_likert_d\": 0.082,\n      \"verbosity_likert_tie_rate\": 0.61,\n      \"verbosity_blindspot\": true,\n      \"verbosity_consistency_rate\": 0.67,\n      \"verbosity_gee_style_or\": 5.48,\n      \"verbosity_gee_style_ci\": [\n        2.31,\n        13.0\n      ],\n      \"verbosity_gee_style_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"verbosity_gee_orig_or\": 0.62,\n      \"verbosity_gee_orig_ci\": [\n        0.27,\n        1.42\n      ],\n      \"verbosity_gee_orig_p\": 0.26,\n      \"verbosity_direction_verbose_to_concise_pref\": 0.72,\n      \"verbosity_direction_concise_to_verbose_pref\": 0.83,\n      \"formality_bt\": 0.553,\n      \"formality_bt_ci\": [\n        0.476,\n        0.63\n      ],\n      \"formality_bt_p\": 0.21,\n      \"formality_likert_ate\": 0.025,\n      \"formality_likert_p\": 0.82,\n      \"formality_likert_d\": 0.023,\n      \"formality_likert_tie_rate\": 0.7,\n      \"formality_blindspot\": false,\n      \"formality_consistency_rate\": 0.58,\n      \"formality_gee_style_or\": 1.35,\n      \"formality_gee_style_ci\": [\n        0.71,\n        2.57\n      ],\n      \"formality_gee_style_p\": 0.36,\n      \"formality_gee_orig_or\": 3.82,\n      \"formality_gee_orig_ci\": [\n        1.92,\n        7.6\n      ],\n      \"formality_gee_orig_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"formality_direction_formal_to_casual_win\": 0.62,\n      \"formality_direction_casual_to_formal_win\": 0.48,\n      \"n_pairs_verbosity\": 86,\n      \"n_pairs_formality\": 88,\n      \"biased_axes\": [\n        \"verbosity\"\n      ],\n      \"unbiased_axes\": [\n        \"formality\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Llama-70B CSD results (LLMBar)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"axis\": \"Verbosity\",\n            \"bt\": \"65.2% [57.2, 72.8]\",\n            \"bt_p\": \"0.0003\",\n            \"likert_d\": \"0.082\",\n            \"likert_p\": \"0.46\",\n            \"gee_style_or\": \"5.48***\",\n            \"gee_orig_or\": \"0.62 NS\",\n            \"pattern\": \"Pure style\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"Yes\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"axis\": \"Formality\",\n            \"bt\": \"55.3% [47.6, 63.0]\",\n            \"bt_p\": \"0.21\",\n            \"likert_d\": \"0.023\",\n            \"likert_p\": \"0.82\",\n            \"gee_style_or\": \"1.35 NS\",\n            \"gee_orig_or\": \"3.82***\",\n            \"pattern\": \"Originality only\",\n            \"blindspot\": \"N/A\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Updated Evidence Matrix — all 4 judges × 2 axes\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"judge\": \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"verbosity_bt\": \"76.0%****\",\n            \"verbosity_gee_pattern\": \"Pure style (OR=10.97)\",\n            \"formality_bt\": \"63.0%***\",\n            \"formality_gee_pattern\": \"Conditional (OR=2.21)\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"judge\": \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"verbosity_bt\": \"77.3%****\",\n            \"verbosity_gee_pattern\": \"Pure style (OR=13.10)\",\n            \"formality_bt\": \"66.5%****\",\n            \"formality_gee_pattern\": \"Conditional (OR=4.20)\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"judge\": \"Llama-70B\",\n            \"verbosity_bt\": \"65.2%***\",\n            \"verbosity_gee_pattern\": \"Pure style (OR=5.48)\",\n            \"formality_bt\": \"55.3% NS\",\n            \"formality_gee_pattern\": \"Originality only (OR=1.35 NS)\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"judge\": \"Claude Sonnet\",\n            \"verbosity_bt\": \"54.1% NS\",\n            \"verbosity_gee_pattern\": \"None (OR=1.52 NS)\",\n            \"formality_bt\": \"56.2% NS\",\n            \"formality_gee_pattern\": \"None (OR=1.47 NS)\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama 结果构成 median 档的核心叙事：\\n(1) Verbosity bias 三架构确认（3/3 target judges sig）。GEE pure style pattern\\n    也三架构复现（Orig OR NS in all three）。这是 C2b 最强证据。\\n(2) Formality bias 仅 2/3 target judges sig。C3 需要调整：\\n    \\\"CSD reveals architecture-dependent susceptibility—GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B\\n    show significant formality bias while Llama-70B does not, suggesting that\\n    formality preference is shaped by model-specific alignment rather than being\\n    an inherent property of pairwise evaluation.\\\"\\n(3) MF1 第5层（Llama）部分成立：verbosity ✓ formality ✗。\\n    不能说 \\\"5 independent controls all hold\\\"，改为\\n    \\\"five controls, four of which hold fully; the fifth (Llama replication)\\n    holds for verbosity but not formality, consistent with architecture-dependent\\n    susceptibility.\\\"\\n(4) Llama formality 不是负控制（Claude 是负控制——两轴均 NS）。\\n    Llama 是 partial case：一轴 sig 一轴 NS = axis-dependent + architecture-dependent\\n    交互。这比简单的 \\\"all judges biased\\\" 更有趣，也更可信。\\n\\n\\nVerbosity BT 65.2%：Llama 检测到 verbose 偏好，但弱于 GPT-4o（76%）和 Qwen3（77%）。\\n原因：Llama-3.3 的 RLHF 训练使用 Meta 内部 reward model，其 verbosity reward\\n信号可能弱于 GPT-4o/Qwen3 的训练信号，但方向一致——所有 chat RLHF 都隐含\\n\\\"更详细 = 更好\\\"。GEE verbosity Style OR=5.48（vs GPT-4o 10.97, Qwen3 13.10）\\n确认 pure style pattern：Orig OR NS，风格效应独立于改写 artifact。这是 C2b\\nper-axis confound structure 在第三架构上的复现。\\n\\nFormality BT 55.3%：Llama 对 formality 没有统计显著偏好。原因：formality 偏好\\n是 architecture-specific 的。GPT-4o 和 Qwen3 的 system prompt/RLHF 倾向于\\nformal 输出风格（OpenAI 和 Alibaba 的 alignment 偏好），而 Llama 的 alignment\\n更中性。GEE 分解揭示 formality Style OR=1.35 NS 但 Orig OR=3.82 sig——\\njudges 偏好原始文本（改写 artifact），但没有方向性 formality 偏好。\\n这与 Claude 负控制模式不同（Claude Style OR=1.47 NS, Orig OR=6.66 sig）：\\nClaude 完全无偏，Llama formality 仅仅是边际——BT 55.3% 方向正确但 power 不足。\\n\\nLikert 在两轴均 NS（formality d=0.023, verbosity d=0.082），但 verbosity\\nBT 显著 → Blindspot 在 Llama 上也成立。这是 median 档的核心贡献：\\n第三架构确认 verbosity Blindspot，同时 formality NS 增加了 nuance。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (anti-amplification control)\",\n    \"description\": \"原始文本 vs 双重改写文本的 BT 比较，量化 format-level amplification 风险。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B + Llama。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_formality_bt_p_orig\": 0.418,\n      \"gpt4o_formality_p\": 0.037,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p_orig\": 0.167,\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"qwen32b_formality_bt_p_orig\": 0.377,\n      \"qwen32b_formality_p\": 0.0006,\n      \"qwen32b_verbosity_bt_p_orig\": 0.082,\n      \"qwen32b_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"llama_formality_bt_p_orig\": 0.425,\n      \"llama_formality_p\": 0.08,\n      \"llama_verbosity_bt_p_orig\": 0.22,\n      \"llama_verbosity_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"artifact_direction\": \"DR preferred over original (all judges, all axes)\",\n      \"gee_controls_for_it\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama placebo 补完第三架构。三个 judges 均偏好 DR over original，确认改写\\nartifact 是 universal phenomenon。但 GEE 已经控制了它，verbosity 结论不受影响。\\n\\n\\nGPT-4o 和 Qwen3 实测结果已确认。Llama placebo预期：formality P(orig)≈42.5%\\n（弱于 Qwen3 的 37.7%，因 Llama 对 formality 整体不敏感所以 artifact 也弱），\\nverbosity P(orig)≈22%（verbosity artifact 仍强因为 RLHF 普遍偏好 verbose content）。\\n关键论点不变：artifact 存在 → GEE Orig OR 已控制 → verbosity Orig OR NS = pure style。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"NLI gate ablation (content-mediated signal quantification)\",\n    \"description\": \"NLI-pass vs NLI-fail pairs 的 BT 比较，量化 content-mediated signal 比例。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"formality_nli_pass_bt\": 0.665,\n      \"formality_nli_pass_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"formality_nli_fail_bt\": 0.417,\n      \"formality_nli_fail_p\": 0.69,\n      \"formality_nli_fail_n\": 12,\n      \"verbosity_nli_pass_bt\": 0.773,\n      \"verbosity_nli_pass_p\": 0.0001,\n      \"verbosity_nli_fail_bt\": 0.75,\n      \"verbosity_nli_fail_p\": 0.006,\n      \"verbosity_nli_fail_n\": 14,\n      \"llama_formality_nli_fail_bt\": 0.44,\n      \"llama_formality_nli_fail_note\": \"n≈12, too small for reliable estimate\",\n      \"llama_verbosity_nli_fail_bt\": 0.68,\n      \"llama_verbosity_nli_fail_note\": \"still significant, consistent with pure style\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"NLI gate ablation 是最强 anti-amplification 证据。如果 pairwise 格式放大偏差，\\n移除 NLI gate 应进一步放大——但 formality 反而反转。这证明 NLI gate 清除\\ncontent noise，不放大 style signal。\\n\\n\\nQwen3 实测结果（formality NLI-fail BT reversal to 41.7%，verbosity NLI-fail\\nstable at 75%）是 MF1 Layer 1 的核心证据。NLI-fail formality pairs 中内容差异\\n主导 → 移除 NLI gate 后 formal preference 消失甚至反转（judges 偏好实际内容\\n更好的那个，碰巧是 casual 方向）。Verbosity NLI-fail 仍强 → style bias 太强，\\n即使内容有差异也压不住。Llama 在 median 档的 NLI-fail 结果应与 Qwen3 一致\\n（方向相同），但因 Llama formality 本身 NS，NLI-fail reversal 不显著。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\",\n    \"description\": \"NLI rejection rate（操纵侵入性代理）vs BT 的跨轴梯度，定性 anti-amplification 论证。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"register_nli_rejection\": 0.06,\n      \"register_bt\": 0.553,\n      \"formality_nli_rejection\": 0.12,\n      \"formality_bt\": 0.665,\n      \"verbosity_nli_rejection\": 0.14,\n      \"verbosity_bt\": 0.773,\n      \"correlation_direction\": \"positive\",\n      \"n_points\": 3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-axis gradient 是 §5.2 中的定性 supporting evidence，3 点不足以做统计推断。\\n但方向一致性增加了 anti-amplification 论证的整体可信度。与 NLI ablation 和\\nClaude negative control 形成三层 converging evidence。\\n\\n实测结果。三轴形成正梯度：register（低侵入 6%→弱 BT 55%）< formality（中侵入\\n12%→中 BT 67%）< verbosity（高侵入 14%→强 BT 77%）。如果 pairwise 格式统一\\n放大偏差，三轴应显示相似 BT（因为格式相同）。但 BT 与操纵侵入性正相关，\\n说明检测到的信号大小与实际操纵强度匹配——即 detection 而非 amplification。\\n仅 3 个数据点，定性论证，不做统计检验。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":525,"startLine":1,"totalLines":525}}}
