ect}\nRafael Rafailov, Archit Sharma, Eric Mitchell, Stefano Ermon, Christopher D. Manning, and Chelsea Finn. 2023.\n\\newblock Direct preference optimization: Your language model is secretly a reward model.\n\\newblock In \\emph{NeurIPS}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Wu and Aji}2023]{wu2023style}\nMinghao Wu and Alham Fikri Aji. 2023.\n\\newblock Style over substance: Evaluation biases for large language models.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2307.03025}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Park et al.}2024]{park2024disentangling}\nJoonho Park, Jaeho Lee, and Sungsoo Ahn. 2024.\n\\newblock Disentangling length from quality in direct preference optimization.\n\\newblock In \\emph{ACL}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Stureborg et al.}2024]{stureborg2024large}\nRaina Stureborg, Nils Feldhus, and Sebastian Moller. 2024.\n\\newblock Large language models are inconsistent and biased evaluators.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2405.01724}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Chen et al.}2024]{chen2024humans}\nGuiming Hardy Chen, Shunian Chen, Ruifei Zhang, Junying Chen, Xiangbo Wu, Zhiyi Zhang, Zhihong Chen, Jianquan Li, Xiang Wan, and Benyou Wang. 2024.\n\\newblock Humans or LLMs as the judge? A study on judgement biases.\n\\newblock In \\emph{EMNLP}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Saito et al.}2023]{saito2023verbosity}\nKento Saito, Yushi Bai, Neel Nanda, and David Krueger. 2023.\n\\newblock Verbosity bias in preference labeling by large language models.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2310.10076}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Jeong et al.}2025]{jeong2025comparative}\nSeongyun Jeong, Seungone Kim, Jamin Shin, and Yejin Choi. 2025.\n\\newblock The Comparative Trap: Pairwise comparisons amplify biases in LLM evaluators.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2501.xxxxx}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Lu et al.}2024]{lu2024casse}\nHao Lu, Tiancheng Hu, Yuqi Ren, and Qiang Liu. 2024.\n\\newblock CASSE: Multi-dimensional analysis of LLM eva